class Solution {
    public int getSecondLargest(int[] arr) {

        int largest = arr[0];
        int slargest = -1; // since while checking it should be smaller than largest,
                           // therefore assigned minimum value (-1) for comparison
                           //can take Integer.MIN_VALUE

        for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {

            if (arr[i] > largest) {
                slargest = largest;
                largest = arr[i];
            }
            else if (arr[i] < largest && arr[i] > slargest) {
                slargest = arr[i];
            }
        }

        return slargest;
    }
}

🧠 Why this is optimal

Time Complexity: O(n) ✅ (single loop)

Space Complexity: O(1) ✅

Technique: Linear traversal + running comparison

No sorting needed (sorting would be O(n log n) ❌)
